CLAMSHELL HALF. ONE DESIGN, TWO COPIES, THE SECOND MIRRORED IN X.
  split face x 0.0, this half x 0.0..12.0; the pair still straddle 24.0
  the bench rejected the monolith TWICE - "worst supports, impossible to clean", then "impossible to print" after the gable. The gable is reverted; the front wall is 4.30 again.
roll servo: case y -12.4..11.3, z -16.6..6.1 | tabs y 4.6, z +/-10.9
J5 SEATING: tab plane y 4.60, agreed with _check_leads MOUNTS. The rotator seats on wro_rot_seat 11.70, NOT on wro_y_front 15.70 - lib/joints.J5_ROTATOR_ORIGIN_PARTS. _check_wrist, _preview_arm and _check_motor_clearance all posed it off the front face until 2026-09-03, 1.30 mm out, which stopped the retaining washer reaching the spline step.
keel: full half width now (was 8.0), y -7.4..8.6, z -23.2..-16.6, bevel 6.6 mm at 45.0 deg
crest: y 5.88..13.92, top 12.70 (z_top 10.84) - THE ONLY ENVELOPE GROWTH, 1.86 mm in +Z over 8.05 mm of Y, to seat one nut
clamshell: 3 x M2 through-bolt, Oe2.40 clearance, seat 4.20 af x 2.40 deep at the bed face (head Oe3.80 OR nut, same recess)
    clamp_keel_aft   y   -5.52  z  -19.50   J4 socket clearance 10.30 mm
    clamp_keel_fwd   y    1.70  z  -19.50   J4 socket clearance 10.30 mm
    clamp_crest      y    9.90  z    9.00   J4 socket clearance 3.87 mm
    the arm's other two clamshells are on M3. This one cannot be: an M3 head is 6.00 across and an M3 nut pocket 5.70, so one recess cannot take both ends and the one-design-mirrored trick fails.
PRINTABILITY - OUTER FACE ON THE BED (x 12.0), BUILT -X, SUPPORT OFF.
  the entire outer form is ONE prism along the build axis, so no outer face is an overhang. Every cavity opens at the top face.
